PrivilegedMode.fluentSetterDocumentation:
/**<p>Enables running the Docker daemon inside a Docker container. Set to true only if the build project is used to build Docker images. Otherwise, a build that attempts to interact with the Docker daemon fails. The default setting is <code>false</code>.</p> <p>You can initialize the Docker daemon during the install phase of your build by adding one of the following sets of commands to the install phase of your buildspec file:</p> <p>If the operating system's base image is Ubuntu Linux:</p> <p> <code>- nohup /usr/local/bin/dockerd --host=unix:///var/run/docker.sock --host=tcp://0.0.0.0:2375 --storage-driver=overlay&amp;</code> </p> <p> <code>- timeout 15 sh -c "until docker info; do echo .; sleep 1; done"</code> </p> <p>If the operating system's base image is Alpine Linux and the previous command does not work, add the <code>-t</code> argument to <code>timeout</code>:</p> <p> <code>- nohup /usr/local/bin/dockerd --host=unix:///var/run/docker.sock --host=tcp://0.0.0.0:2375 --storage-driver=overlay&amp;</code> </p> <p> <code>- timeout -t 15 sh -c "until docker info; do echo .; sleep 1; done"</code> </p>
@param privilegedMode Enables running the Docker daemon inside a Docker container. Set to true only if the build project is used to build Docker images. Otherwise, a build that attempts to interact with the Docker daemon fails. The default setting is <code>false</code>.</p> <p>You can initialize the Docker daemon during the install phase of your build by adding one of the following sets of commands to the install phase of your buildspec file:</p> <p>If the operating system's base image is Ubuntu Linux:</p> <p> <code>- nohup /usr/local/bin/dockerd --host=unix:///var/run/docker.sock --host=tcp://0.0.0.0:2375 --storage-driver=overlay&amp;</code> </p> <p> <code>- timeout 15 sh -c "until docker info; do echo .; sleep 1; done"</code> </p> <p>If the operating system's base image is Alpine Linux and the previous command does not work, add the <code>-t</code> argument to <code>timeout</code>:</p> <p> <code>- nohup /usr/local/bin/dockerd --host=unix:///var/run/docker.sock --host=tcp://0.0.0.0:2375 --storage-driver=overlay&amp;</code> </p> <p> <code>- timeout -t 15 sh -c "until docker info; do echo .; sleep 1; done"</code>
